# Inventory Item Unit Conversion
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Warehouse — how many of an Item's Base Unit equal one alternate unit
# Case 5 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# References: inventory-item.menata
#
# Split out from inventory-item.menata (Study 15 Tier 2, corrected 2026-07-11):
# originally written inline on Item as a provisional `Table of (...)` field,
# believing no Language grammar existed for "an Item has several of these." It
# already did — this is the ordinary Object References pattern (001-object.md
# §Relationships): "an Item has many Unit Conversions" is implied by "each Unit
# Conversion references one Item," the same shape accounting-journal-entry-
# line.menata already used correctly. Only Cement-shaped items (Tier 2, multiple
# alternate units) need any rows here at all — Rice-shaped items (Tier 1, one fixed
# pair) hold their conversion as two flat fields elsewhere and need none.

Item Unit Conversion

Fields

- Item : Item
- Unit : PCS | KG | BOX | SAK
- Factor : Number

Constraints

- Unit is required.
- Factor must be greater than zero.

    A Unit may appear only once per Item.

Permissions

Warehouse Staff

- View

Views

- Unit Conversion List : List
- Unit Conversion Detail : Detail
